Start admin website

    cd ~/DETECT-CO/admin_web
    npm run dev

Start laptop-hosted ML API and temporary HTTPS tunnel

    cd ~/DETECT-CO-ML
    bash ./start-tunnel.sh

Keep the tunnel terminal open. The script publishes each verified new URL to
Firebase automatically. Start Flutter normally; the app also syncs the latest
URL at startup and when resumed:

    cd ~/DETECT-CO
    flutter run

Stop the API and tunnel with Ctrl-C in the tunnel terminal, or from another
terminal run:

    cd ~/DETECT-CO-ML
    bash ./stop-tunnel.sh

Start notification listener

    cd ~/DETECT-CO
    node functions/announcement-listener.js


When you restart your server:

Run:

cd ~/DETECT-CO-ML
bash ./start-tunnel.sh

Cloudflare may generate a new URL.

Your script should automatically publish that URL to Firebase.

DETECT-CO users should retrieve the updated URL from Firebase.

You only need to run the manual publishing command if automatic publishing fails:

cd ~/DETECT-CO/functions
npm run publish-ml-api-url -- https://YOUR-NEW-URL.trycloudflare.com